1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,159
It is a most miserable thing to feel ashamed of home.

2
00:00:08,158 --> 00:00:11,680
There may be black ingratitude in the thing, and the punishment may be

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:18,079
retributive and well deserved; but that it is a miserable thing, I can testify.

4
00:00:18,079 --> 00:00:23,558
Home had never been a very pleasant place to me, because of my sister’s temper. But,

5
00:00:23,559 --> 00:00:30,600
Joe had sanctified it, and I had believed in it. I had believed in the best parlour as a most elegant

6
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:37,359
saloon; I had believed in the front door, as a mysterious portal of the Temple of State whose

7
00:00:37,359 --> 00:00:44,040
solemn opening was attended with a sacrifice of roast fowls; I had believed in the kitchen as

8
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:50,040
a chaste though not magnificent apartment; I had believed in the forge as the glowing

9
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:56,199
road to manhood and independence. Within a single year all this was changed. Now it was

10
00:00:56,199 --> 00:01:02,558
all coarse and common, and I would not have had Miss Havisham and Estella see it on any account.

11
00:01:02,559 --> 00:01:07,478
How much of my ungracious condition of mind may have been my own fault,

12
00:01:07,478 --> 00:01:13,879
how much Miss Havisham’s, how much my sister’s, is now of no moment to me or to any one. The

13
00:01:13,879 --> 00:01:22,559
change was made in me; the thing was done. Well or ill done, excusably or inexcusably, it was done.

14
00:01:22,559 --> 00:01:27,600
Once, it had seemed to me that when I should at last roll up my shirt-sleeves and go into the

15
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:35,279
forge, Joe’s ’prentice, I should be distinguished and happy. Now the reality was in my hold,

16
00:01:35,279 --> 00:01:40,638
I only felt that I was dusty with the dust of small-coal, and that I had a weight upon

17
00:01:40,639 --> 00:01:46,959
my daily remembrance to which the anvil was a feather. There have been occasions in my

18
00:01:46,959 --> 00:01:52,760
later life (I suppose as in most lives) when I have felt for a time as if a thick curtain

19
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:58,318
had fallen on all its interest and romance, to shut me out from anything save dull endurance

20
00:01:58,318 --> 00:02:04,040
any more. Never has that curtain dropped so heavy and blank, as when my way in life lay

21
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:10,359
stretched out straight before me through the newly entered road of apprenticeship to Joe.

22
00:02:10,359 --> 00:02:15,959
I remember that at a later period of my “time,” I used to stand about the churchyard on Sunday

23
00:02:15,959 --> 00:02:22,719
evenings when night was falling, comparing my own perspective with the windy marsh view,

24
00:02:22,719 --> 00:02:27,600
and making out some likeness between them by thinking how flat and low both were,

25
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:33,799
and how on both there came an unknown way and a dark mist and then the sea. I was

26
00:02:33,799 --> 00:02:39,120
quite as dejected on the first working-day of my apprenticeship as in that after-time;

27
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:45,558
but I am glad to know that I never breathed a murmur to Joe while my indentures lasted.

28
00:02:45,559 --> 00:02:49,600
It is about the only thing I am glad to know of myself in that connection.

29
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:56,520
For, though it includes what I proceed to add, all the merit of what I proceed to add was Joe’s. It

30
00:02:56,520 --> 00:03:02,000
was not because I was faithful, but because Joe was faithful, that I never ran away and went for

31
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,120
a soldier or a sailor. It was not because I had a strong sense of the virtue of industry,

32
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:15,398
but because Joe had a strong sense of the virtue of industry, that I worked with tolerable zeal

33
00:03:15,398 --> 00:03:22,120
against the grain. It is not possible to know how far the influence of any amiable

34
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:29,199
honest-hearted duty-doing man flies out into the world; but it is very possible to know how it has

35
00:03:29,199 --> 00:03:34,519
touched one’s self in going by, and I know right well that any good that intermixed itself with

36
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:42,359
my apprenticeship came of plain contented Joe, and not of restlessly aspiring discontented me.

37
00:03:42,359 --> 00:03:49,599
What I wanted, who can say? How can I say, when I never knew? What I dreaded was,

38
00:03:49,600 --> 00:04:06,911
that in some unlucky hour I, being at my grimiest and commonest, should lift up my

39
00:04:06,911 --> 00:04:07,003
eyes and see Estella looking in at one of the wooden windows of the forge. I was haunted by

40
00:04:07,003 --> 00:04:07,799
the fear that she would, sooner or later, find me out, with a black face and hands,

41
00:04:07,799 --> 00:04:15,840
doing the coarsest part of my work, and would exult over me and despise me. Often after dark,

42
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:21,040
when I was pulling the bellows for Joe, and we were singing Old Clem, and when the thought how

43
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:26,600
we used to sing it at Miss Havisham’s would seem to show me Estella’s face in the fire,

44
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:32,478
with her pretty hair fluttering in the wind and her eyes scorning me,—often at such a time I

45
00:04:32,478 --> 00:04:37,879
would look towards those panels of black night in the wall which the wooden windows then were, and

46
00:04:37,879 --> 00:04:45,079
would fancy that I saw her just drawing her face away, and would believe that she had come at last.

47
00:04:45,079 --> 00:04:49,519
After that, when we went in to supper, the place and the meal would have a more

48
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:53,840
homely look than ever, and I would feel more ashamed of home than ever,

49
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:57,000
in my own ungracious breast. Chapter 15.
